# Files Prettier must not touch (issue #97).
#
# The rule: if something other than a human writes the file, the formatter and that writer will
# fight, and the loser is `pnpm run format:check` — permanently red for a reason nobody can fix by
# hand. Everything below has a generator; everything else in the repo gets formatted.

# Palette Press goldens. Written by the test itself as `JSON.stringify(payload, null, 2) + "\n"`
# (packages/palette-press/test/golden.test.ts, via `pnpm --filter @marquee/palette-press
# run update-goldens`). Prettier's JSON style differs, so formatting them means the next golden
# refresh reverts it and the check goes red again. A golden's whole value is being byte-identical to
# what the generator produces — reformatting one is how you make it meaningless.
fixtures/palettes/*.golden.json

# pnpm's lockfile: generated, ordered by the resolver, and merged by pnpm's own strategy.
pnpm-lock.yaml

# The Curator design handoff (ADR 0052). Written by the design tool, in a bespoke streaming-HTML
# component format whose inline styles are one-per-line by construction — prettier expands every one
# of them into a block, which is a 10x diff that makes the reference unreadable and would be undone
# the moment a new bundle is exported. `support.js` and `image-slot.js` are that tool's runtime, not
# our code. These are read, never edited: nothing here is ours to format.
docs/design_handoff_curator_overhaul/

# Build output and dependencies (also gitignored; listed so a local build doesn't slow the check).
node_modules/
dist/
dist-ui/
.turbo/
packages/contracts/ts/*.d.ts
packages/desktop/staged/
packages/desktop/release/
